# Terrain And Biome Integrity

Apply these checks when editing terrain, biomes, chunk generation, or biome-related types.

## Core Constraints

- Keep `src/terrain/**` pure: no `THREE`, no DOM APIs, no side effects.
- Treat chunk payload shape as a contract between `src/terrain/index.ts`, `src/chunk.worker.ts`, and `src/game.ts`.
- Prefer named exports in TypeScript modules.
- Keep new comments and user-facing text in English.

## Biome Change Checklist

When adding or renaming a biome, update all of the following in the same change:

1. `Biome` union in `src/types.ts`
2. Biome file in `src/terrain/biomes/<biome_name>.ts` (snake_case filename)
3. `BIOME_TERRAIN` and `BIOME_LAYERS` registry entries in `src/terrain/biomes/index.ts`
4. `ALL_BIOMES` in `src/terrain/biomes/registry.test.ts`

## Validation Before Finishing

- Run `npm run test:run` when biome registry, terrain params, or layer config changed.
- Run `npm run build` when worker payload, type contracts, or cross-module signatures changed.
